  "provenance": "Retained Sega-derived graphics/font/poses/music/effects converted to native Amiga formats. Private repository retention explicitly approved. No ownership, public redistribution or clean-room claim. CT12 intentionally edits title/logo and status/mode labels using the retained native font. Original imported hashes remain recorded; player-linked palette becomes Red without changing poses or unrelated court colours. Conversion generators/source media live only in Git history/external private inputs. CT13 removes superseded Sega-derived victory score-2/3 from active inputs and supplies the user-selected independently arranged historical Battle Hymn chorus, with independent waveform, accompaniment and period table. Other retained assets keep their stated provenance. Classic human/robot body masks are ImageGen-authored and fitted to retained pose bounds/seams; white rackets, poses, ball/shadow retain Sega-derived provenance. A/B headings retain their native lettering; centred HUMAN/AI role labels use the retained font. Residual court/unused-atlas Sega logo pixels are removed without changing provenance. Plain retained point/advantage glyphs and six compact WIN rows with an open white frame are authored native UI edits; font columns are packed without resampling. No conceptual ImageGen pixels are imported into the scoreboard.",
